5710468226181001-377fc7ae-7fb1-4250-b910-dcb2e600b8c1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"04935cffa60c37f6a091f186d8eb7f9b055250ca70d2c7f6cd611f1c2db3ff19","event_uuid":"cf753c78-0bce-448c-80c7-6669daed53d3","position":{"commit_sha":"9bd10ac7e9cfadaa7ce7da3336f681f8fd12ccb2","position":"1785710578301667001-cf753c78-0bce-448c-80c7-6669daed53d3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c76c0bbc7e282f7224da67094d9c06234b8c847fbe73f782fa046c492edbebf7","event_uuid":"b13a937c-bd7e-48ff-bd5e-fa9f640c8ac2","position":{"commit_sha":"9bd10ac7e9cfadaa7ce7da3336f681f8fd12ccb2","position":"1785710579168933001-b13a937c-bd7e-48ff-bd5e-fa9f640c8ac2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"e4ff696d-43b7-4303-8b3b-ae64d74a6873","comments":[],"created_at":1785642195810585001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8c2ab8b0-364c-4dc2-9a66-5544349c0e3b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb"}],"description":"# Close the Cloud <-> Data Center reconciler test-parity gaps\n\n## Why this exists\n\nTwo Jira adapters now sit behind one backend port, and they were hardened at different times by\ndifferent means:\n\n* **Cloud** (`adapters/jira/`, ACLI-based) is the historically battle-tested path. Years of\n  production incidents produced byte-for-byte characterization pins, ADF depth tests, comment and\n  description length-convergence suites, and a large applier/differ corpus.\n* **Data Center** (`adapters/jira_datacenter/`, pycontribs-based) was written and tested intensively\n  during epic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb], which drove it against a real Dockerized instance. That\n  work produced things Cloud never had: multi-page pagination proofs, a 429/`Retry-After` matrix,\n  TLS and credential validation, a live 49-cell harness suite, and a structural anti-regression\n  guard.\n\n**The gaps therefore run in BOTH directions, and that is the point of this epic.** A parity audit\ncommissioned while closing e369 found Cloud-only coverage that DC lacks AND DC-only coverage that\nCloud lacks — and the second direction contains the single highest-risk finding, because Cloud's\nwhole-project readers have never been tested past one page while DC's have.\n\n## The governing insight\n\nEvery defect e369 found in the DC adapter was an OPERATIONAL EDGE that only appears against a\ndifferently-configured instance: index lag, server-side page caps, admin-toggled rate limiting,\nscreen configuration, workflow transition naming. None was an architectural flaw. The same class of\nedge exists on Cloud and is simply untested there, because Cloud's coverage grew from *incidents\nthat happened* rather than from *configurations that differ*.\n\nSo this epic is not \"make the two suites look alike\". It is: **for each behaviour the two adapters\nshare, the harder-won test should exist on both sides**, and where a SHARED module is exercised\nthrough only one adapter, a regression must not be able to reach production for the other.\n\n## Scope\n\nTest-tier work plus the small production changes that untested duplication forces (one map is\ngenuinely duplicated and must be single-sourced before it can be guarded). No behaviour change to\neither adapter is intended; where a test reveals one is needed, that becomes its own bug ticket\nrather than being folded in silently.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nAdding coverage for behaviours only one adapter HAS (Cloud's ADF codec depth, DC's TLS/PAT\nhandling) — those are legitimate asymmetries, not gaps. Promoting `_engine` through the mypy\nstrictness ratchet. Any change to the backend port's shape.\n\n## Provenance\n\nCommissioned during epic e369's closeout. Every finding below was verified against the tree before\nbeing written down — the audit was treated as a lead, not as evidence.\n\n## PRIORITY FRAMING (operator direction, 2026-08-02) — READ THIS BEFORE PICKING UP A CHILD\n\nThe top priority is **shipping defect-free Jira Data Center functionality.** This epic is a\n*related* priority precisely because parity is what gives confidence that the DC feature is\ndefect-free — it is instrumental to the goal, not adjacent to it.\n\nThat ranks the two directions differently, and the ranking should drive which child you take:\n\n* **DC-DIRECTION GAPS COME FIRST.** `cedc` (DC characterization) and `79d5` (DC length convergence\n  + the comment ceiling) are the ones that directly buy confidence in what is being shipped. DC's\n  values have never been pinned; its contract test asserts SHAPE only and would pass with every\n  value wrong. Until those land, \"the DC adapter is defect-free\" rests on the live harness alone,\n  and the live harness only covers the configurations that one default-configured instance happens\n  to have.\n* **BOTH-DIRECTION items rank with them** where they touch DC: `bd9e` (the duplicated ticket-type\n  map is read by DC's create path) and `2944` (several of the tests that cannot fail are DC tests,\n  so they are confidence we do not actually have).\n* **CLOUD-DIRECTION GAPS RANK BELOW.** `0fad` and `2127` harden the mature, live-exercised Cloud\n  path. They are real and worth doing — `0fad` in particular is a genuine latent truncation risk —\n  but they do not serve the DC-confidence goal, and they must not gate it. `0fad` was moved out of\n  epic e369 for exactly this reason and dropped to P2 under this framing.\n\n**Do not read \"parity\" as \"make the two suites symmetrical.\"** The goal is confidence in the DC\nfeature. Where an asymmetry is legitimate (Cloud's ADF depth, DC's TLS/PAT handling) closing it buys\nnothing.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `cedc-58d1-f6d1-428e` is closed: DC's create-path field values, both sanitizer boundaries,\n      the identity label form, and all four probe branches are pinned BY VALUE, and the shared\n      `map_fields_to_remote` body is exercised through `WikiTextCodec` as well as `AdfCodec`\n- [ ] `79d5-63c7-5f31-48a7` is closed: an oversized DC comment AND an oversized DC description each\n      converge across TWO passes (pass 2 plans nothing for that ticket), and the DC comment\n      ceiling's PROVENANCE is cited in the source at the `max_chars=WIKI_DESCRIPTION_LIMIT` binding\n      — naming `jira.text.field.character.limit` and JRASERVER-28519 — so the constant reads as a\n      decision rather than an assumption. (The ceiling is no longer unknown: it was established from\n      Jira's `jpm.xml`, whose property description covers Comments as well as Description; that it\n      is admin-configurable is tracked separately as `049e-9fac-a821-4ea2` and does NOT gate this\n      epic.) Verified by reading the cited comment in the diff\n- [ ] `bd9e-0740-1b47-47f8` is closed: exactly ONE dict literal defines the local->Jira ticket-type\n      map within `adapters/`, and `test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py` carries an assertion that\n      fails the build if a second copy appears — the same guard shape the status and priority maps\n      already have\n- [ ] `2944-dd3f-e982-4359` is closed: each of the five enumerated vacuous tests either asserts the\n      contract its own docstring names or is renamed to what it actually pins; none is merely\n      deleted, because the docstring's intent is the valuable part\n- [ ] [operator-attested] every pin or rewrite added under this epic is MUTATION-CHECKED — the\n      mutation applied and the resulting verdict recorded as a comment on the owning child ticket. A\n      pin nobody has seen fail is not evidence. Copied terminal output showing the mutated code and\n      the resulting FAIL, pasted as a child-ticket comment, satisfies this criterion; it is attested\n      rather than CI-checkable because a mutation is applied and reverted in a working tree and\n      therefore leaves no repo artifact to inspect\n- [ ] where the two adapters CORRECTLY diverge, the expectation carries a DIFFERENT value per\n      vendor rather than asserting sameness. Checked positively rather than as a negative property:\n      the parametrized characterization suite must contain at least one case for EACH known\n      divergence — (a) rich text, ADF vs wiki markup, and (b) identity form, Cloud `accountId` vs\n      DC `name` — in which the Cloud and DC parameters carry DIFFERENT expected values, and both\n      cases pass. Verifiable by reading the parametrize table in the diff and by running those\n      cases; a reviewer can confirm it without re-deriving which behaviours diverge, because the\n      two are enumerated here\n- [ ] `test_backend_characterization.py`'s pre-existing Cloud assertions still pass UNEDITED, so\n      Cloud's incident-hardened safety net is intact rather than loosened to fit DC","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"cf753c78-0bce-448c-80c7-6669daed53d3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3e73-72b5-cff2-40f0","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Close the Cloud<->DC reconciler test-parity gaps","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["94d10d6e-94c3-4213-bfd8-6f47c4c136bb","8c2ab8b0-364c-4dc2-9a66-5544349c0e3b","f27ade08-3e44-44e7-bd47-3bd78f610dad","1cca4b98-4200-43ad-85e8-e2f847a67db7","b2929b77-45f5-4e94-975d-d5adca047fc9","280bff4b-4d92-4417-8d72-9801e5ac4fb5","88e3ac12-2810-4a35-bac6-0a8268c010d3","377fc7ae-7fb1-4250-b910-dcb2e600b8c1","cf753c78-0bce-448c-80c7-6669daed53d3","b13a937c-bd7e-48ff-bd5e-fa9f640c8ac2"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785710579168933002,"uuid":"9993f9f7-1db9-4e27-bfae-b67c2bd03cfd"}